      "text": "Rippling system design questions: ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Rippling system design questions: ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TJKr77hvUT_omeVFsLSLc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13358.020160417043,
      "y": -4304.287404842213,
      "width": 3388,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aQ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 417389482,
      "version": 1002,
      "versionNonce": 663029617,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763210837706,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Google News Like Aggregator.\n2. Design a news aggregator app with personalised feeds based on user interest and liking of publication house.\n\n3. Design an event system like amplitude with analytics and reporting use cases.\n10. Design metrics system . \n11. Had to design and explain a Rollup-Aggregation system for events- Given: Client sdks that send events & Server that listens to events- Requirements:    - Optimized sent events using batching    - Handle failing requests using idempotency    - Use Rollup-Aggregation at server to store 15m, 1hr, 1day data\n7. Stock price rule notification\n\n4. News feed generation like twitter/instagram.\n5. Design twitter/instagram. \n8. Design a system where Rippling's customers can upload documents for review by internal audit team. Each document has a time to review complete.\n\n\n6. Hotel booking system./ booking system\n9. hotel reservation aggregtor.\n12. Design hotel reservation system like Expedia. Focus on- Searching for rooms by date and location- Reserving rooms- Rooms availability ingestion from 3rd party hotels\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Google News Like Aggregator.\n2. Design a news aggregator app with personalised feeds based on user interest and liking of publication house.\n\n3. Design an event system like amplitude with analytics and reporting use cases.\n10. Design metrics system . \n11. Had to design and explain a Rollup-Aggregation system for events- Given: Client sdks that send events & Server that listens to events- Requirements:    - Optimized sent events using batching    - Handle failing requests using idempotency    - Use Rollup-Aggregation at server to store 15m, 1hr, 1day data\n7. Stock price rule notification\n\n4. News feed generation like twitter/instagram.\n5. Design twitter/instagram. \n8. Design a system where Rippling's customers can upload documents for review by internal audit team. Each document has a time to review complete.\n\n\n6. Hotel booking system./ booking system\n9. hotel reservation aggregtor.\n12. Design hotel reservation system like Expedia. Focus on- Searching for rooms by date and location- Reserving rooms- Rooms availability ingestion from 3rd party hotels\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nC9kmtSXrlpl3pHZ73LFr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3230.2095016006006,
      "y": -3671.506006228437,
      "width": 3606.767578125,
      "height": 8957.17619234742,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aR",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1839860522,
      "version": 4525,
      "versionNonce": 842185631,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763266600433,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Google News Like Aggregator. -> https://www.systemdesignhandbook.com/guides/google-news-system-design/\n\n\nFR: \n- Show the news from multiple third publishers like ndtv, firstpost etc, \n- based on users interest, subscription, liking of categories, view etc .\n- also categories each news in different categories and show to users. \n- apart from this user can also subscribe news to certain categories like education, or publishers say ndtv.\n\nDoubts: \n- should we assume third party publisher providing api or ? \n- like web sraping we want to do ? \n- RSS feed ( really simple syndication ) \n- all three type of integration possible depdening upon publisher\n\n\nNFR: \n\n- do we want to have 100% consistency in news or availability -> availability >> eventual consistency.\n- how much delay is OK in news showing from publisher to this system. \n- retention/durability of these news -> old ? \n- no duplicate article scrape.\n- group the same/duplicte news from multiple publisherss.\n- ranking -> recency , location trending, global trending, interest. \n- spam/anomaly news filtering.  \n- alerts, monitoring, rate limiting, pagers\n\n\nEstimations;\n- Publisher counts: 1k \n- avg news publish to a publisher counts: 50 / day\n- avg user feed requests , 5/day\n- total MAU -> 10M \n- avg qps -> DAU -> 1k -> per day -> 5k query\n- qps -> 200 -> peak -> 5x -> 1k/s for feed\n- Storage -> \n\n\nEntities: \n- Publisher, Content, Subscription, User, Feed\n\nApi Designing: \n- Data ingestion\n    - Add publisher\n    - /api/v1/publisher -> POST, x-token -> authoriser\n      Req: {Publiser}, Res: 2xx\n- Subscribe to publisher:\n    - /api/v1/publisher/subscribe?id=\"\" -> GET, x-token \n      Res: 2xx\n- similary to unsubscribe:\n\n- Specific Category Feed:\n- Feed generation: \n    - api/v1/feed/ --> POST x-token\n  Req: { filters: { categoryType, location}, pagesize: <>, cursor: <> }\nfor user -> category -> 'YOU', else 'SPORT' etc.\n\n\n- View content: \n- Like content: \n\n  - api/v1/content/id/view=\"\"&&publishser=\"\"\n  - api/v1/content/id/like=\"\"&&publishser=\"\"\n\n\n\n\nDb Schema Designing: \n\nPublisher:\n    - Id\n    - integration details -> RSS/API/SCRAPE\n        - ratetime etc details.\n        - api etc. \n    - createdTime\n\nContentCategory\n    - Id\n    - name\n    \nContent: \n    - Id\n    - publisherId\n    - contentCategoryId\n    - hash\n    - thumbnailUrl: \n    - title\n    - redirectionLink\n    - location\n    - semantic -> help to group same kind of news.\n\nUser:\n    - Id\n\n\nOLAP:\n\nUserContentLike\n    - Id\n    - contentId\n\nUserContentView\n    - Id\n    - contentId\n\netc. later if time left\n\nUserInterest:\n    - Id\n    - userId\n    - topKCategoryId\n    - topKSematicId\n\n\n\n    \n\n",
      "fontSize": 60.72661825320286,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Google News Like Aggregator. -> https://www.systemdesignhandbook.com/guides/google-news-system-design/\n\n\nFR: \n- Show the news from multiple third publishers like ndtv, firstpost etc, \n- based on users interest, subscription, liking of categories, view etc .\n- also categories each news in different categories and show to users. \n- apart from this user can also subscribe news to certain categories like education, or publishers say ndtv.\n\nDoubts: \n- should we assume third party publisher providing api or ? \n- like web sraping we want to do ? \n- RSS feed ( really simple syndication ) \n- all three type of integration possible depdening upon publisher\n\n\nNFR: \n\n- do we want to have 100% consistency in news or availability -> availability >> eventual consistency.\n- how much delay is OK in news showing from publisher to this system. \n- retention/durability of these news -> old ? \n- no duplicate article scrape.\n- group the same/duplicte news from multiple publisherss.\n- ranking -> recency , location trending, global trending, interest. \n- spam/anomaly news filtering.  \n- alerts, monitoring, rate limiting, pagers\n\n\nEstimations;\n- Publisher counts: 1k \n- avg news publish to a publisher counts: 50 / day\n- avg user feed requests , 5/day\n- total MAU -> 10M \n- avg qps -> DAU -> 1k -> per day -> 5k query\n- qps -> 200 -> peak -> 5x -> 1k/s for feed\n- Storage -> \n\n\nEntities: \n- Publisher, Content, Subscription, User, Feed\n\nApi Designing: \n- Data ingestion\n    - Add publisher\n    - /api/v1/publisher -> POST, x-token -> authoriser\n      Req: {Publiser}, Res: 2xx\n- Subscribe to publisher:\n    - /api/v1/publisher/subscribe?id=\"\" -> GET, x-token \n      Res: 2xx\n- similary to unsubscribe:\n\n- Specific Category Feed:\n- Feed generation: \n    - api/v1/feed/ --> POST x-token\n  Req: { filters: { categoryType, location}, pagesize: <>, cursor: <> }\nfor user -> category -> 'YOU', else 'SPORT' etc.\n\n\n- View content: \n- Like content: \n\n  - api/v1/content/id/view=\"\"&&publishser=\"\"\n  - api/v1/content/id/like=\"\"&&publishser=\"\"\n\n\n\n\nDb Schema Designing: \n\nPublisher:\n    - Id\n    - integration details -> RSS/API/SCRAPE\n        - ratetime etc details.\n        - api etc. \n    - createdTime\n\nContentCategory\n    - Id\n    - name\n    \nContent: \n    - Id\n    - publisherId\n    - contentCategoryId\n    - hash\n    - thumbnailUrl: \n    - title\n    - redirectionLink\n    - location\n    - semantic -> help to group same kind of news.\n\nUser:\n    - Id\n\n\nOLAP:\n\nUserContentLike\n    - Id\n    - contentId\n\nUserContentView\n    - Id\n    - contentId\n\netc. later if time left\n\nUserInterest:\n    - Id\n    - userId\n    - topKCategoryId\n    - topKSematicId\n\n\n\n    \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
