    {
      "id": "pfwuswJnWy7atfcr-9Pm2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20957.347250202067,
      "y": -3486.952866031264,
      "width": 765.5989379882812,
      "height": 80,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 143142591,
      "version": 119,
      "versionNonce": 824522321,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763217179756,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. Hotel booking system./ booking system\n9. hotel reservation aggregtor.\n12. Design hotel reservation system like Expedia. Focus on- Searching for rooms by date\nand location- Reserving rooms- Rooms availability ingestion from 3rd party hotels",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6. Hotel booking system./ booking system\n9. hotel reservation aggregtor.\n12. Design hotel reservation system like Expedia. Focus on- Searching for rooms by date and location- Reserving rooms- Rooms availability ingestion from 3rd party hotels",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "mxhD67iy6cR2AqQTDekJv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20966.627470132808,
      "y": -3317.9742524324797,
      "width": 1152.798583984375,
      "height": 1980,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 305722929,
      "version": 3173,
      "versionNonce": 1957446705,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763217179756,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FR: \n- Typical Hotel management reservation -> room date range booking etc. - also make booking for the bus booking.\n    - Searching for rooms by date and location\n    - Reserving rooms\n    - Rooms availability ingestion from 3rd party hotels\n- that the hotel can be listed on other aggregators as well and we need to handle this. -> basically what if there is only one room\n  it is booked by expedia customer, how will airbnb will know this ? \n\nFR: \n- user should be able to search hotels by date , location etc. \n- user should be able to booking the rooms of hotel in date range etc. \n- also handle how our platform will have hotels ingestion , admin cases. \n- think this case , if hotel is available on other aggregator as well like AirBnb as hotel owner as well as platform. \n- how admin will update hotels ?? -> is it admin will update inventory or poll something ? \n\nBonus: \n- Should we take payment system as third party right ? and assume as black box ? \n\nNFR: \n- consistency -> avoid the double booking risk. \n- also system to be idempotent. \n- scalable and highly available in case of search \n\n\nEstimations: \n- MAU -> \n- Seaching QPS , peak \n- booking QPS , peak \n- Storage -> \n\nEntities: \n- User , hotel, reservation, inventory, payment\n\nApi Designing: \n- listing: \n  /api/v1/search/hotels  POST\n\nx-token: <> \nRequest: {\n   requestMeta: {}\n   filter: {}\n   pageSize: {}\n   offset or cursor: <> \n\n}\n\nx-track-id , status code: 2xx, 4xx, 5xx etc. \nResponse: {\n   pagesize: <> \n   cusor: <> \n   hotels: [{hotel1, hotel2, ..... }]\n}\n\n- CRUD hotels:\n\n- api/v1/hotel/?id=<>     GET\n- api/v1/hotel/           PUT Req: {hotel}, Response: status \n- api/v1/hotel/?id=<>     DELETE\n- api/v1/hotel/           POST Req: {hotel}, Response: hotel\n\n- Similarly for hotel's room. \n- similarly for hotel's room inventory.\n\n\nDatabase Schema: \n\n- User\n     - Id uuid PK\n     - md\n\n- Hotel\n     - Id \n     - md\n\n- HotelRoomType \n    - Id \n    - hotelId  (1:m) \n    - typeId\n    - md \n\n- RoomType\n    - Id \n\n- HotelRoomInventoryPrice\n    - Id\n    - hotelRoomInventoryId\n    - date\n    - hotelRoomTypeId\n\n- HotelRoomInventory\n    - Id\n    - hotelRoomTypeId\n    - hotelId \n    - totalCounts\n    - date  // for future date as well. \n               basically per day inventory. \n    - availableCounts\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FR: \n- Typical Hotel management reservation -> room date range booking etc. - also make booking for the bus booking.\n    - Searching for rooms by date and location\n    - Reserving rooms\n    - Rooms availability ingestion from 3rd party hotels\n- that the hotel can be listed on other aggregators as well and we need to handle this. -> basically what if there is only one room\n  it is booked by expedia customer, how will airbnb will know this ? \n\nFR: \n- user should be able to search hotels by date , location etc. \n- user should be able to booking the rooms of hotel in date range etc. \n- also handle how our platform will have hotels ingestion , admin cases. \n- think this case , if hotel is available on other aggregator as well like AirBnb as hotel owner as well as platform. \n- how admin will update hotels ?? -> is it admin will update inventory or poll something ? \n\nBonus: \n- Should we take payment system as third party right ? and assume as black box ? \n\nNFR: \n- consistency -> avoid the double booking risk. \n- also system to be idempotent. \n- scalable and highly available in case of search \n\n\nEstimations: \n- MAU -> \n- Seaching QPS , peak \n- booking QPS , peak \n- Storage -> \n\nEntities: \n- User , hotel, reservation, inventory, payment\n\nApi Designing: \n- listing: \n  /api/v1/search/hotels  POST\n\nx-token: <> \nRequest: {\n   requestMeta: {}\n   filter: {}\n   pageSize: {}\n   offset or cursor: <> \n\n}\n\nx-track-id , status code: 2xx, 4xx, 5xx etc. \nResponse: {\n   pagesize: <> \n   cusor: <> \n   hotels: [{hotel1, hotel2, ..... }]\n}\n\n- CRUD hotels:\n\n- api/v1/hotel/?id=<>     GET\n- api/v1/hotel/           PUT Req: {hotel}, Response: status \n- api/v1/hotel/?id=<>     DELETE\n- api/v1/hotel/           POST Req: {hotel}, Response: hotel\n\n- Similarly for hotel's room. \n- similarly for hotel's room inventory.\n\n\nDatabase Schema: \n\n- User\n     - Id uuid PK\n     - md\n\n- Hotel\n     - Id \n     - md\n\n- HotelRoomType \n    - Id \n    - hotelId  (1:m) \n    - typeId\n    - md \n\n- RoomType\n    - Id \n\n- HotelRoomInventoryPrice\n    - Id\n    - hotelRoomInventoryId\n    - date\n    - hotelRoomTypeId\n\n- HotelRoomInventory\n    - Id\n    - hotelRoomTypeId\n    - hotelId \n    - totalCounts\n    - date  // for future date as well. \n               basically per day inventory. \n    - availableCounts\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "VzBhdmmqzW2In82lBcVjw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 21428.625617940106,
      "y": -2033.6221506971233,
      "width": 272.79962158203125,
      "height": 560,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3M",
