      "versionNonce": 1122166015,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763259276516,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Storage: eventsize: 1kb\n-> 5k/s -> 5mb/s \n-> ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Storage: eventsize: 1kb\n-> 5k/s -> 5mb/s \n-> ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "P2tA1HiSAIo58qH95JMXn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20511.910806933563,
      "y": -8212.88049850565,
      "width": 1478.7408092614687,
      "height": 391.1130698446312,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bEB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1383972177,
      "version": 948,
      "versionNonce": 965567313,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763262900296,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a system where a user can have X favourite stocks and has subscribed to their changes. User will set some rules for price\ndrop/ price rise above a threshold or % value and if the rule is satisfied then we have to sent notificaiton to user.\n\nFor eg: let say user have subscribed to ABC stock and set rule that if stock price goes above 100$ send me notification.\n\nTypes of rules can be - opening price, current price, moving average, etc.\nUser should get the notification within a minute.\nSystem should be able to scan and check more than 1 million rules set by users and send notification if any rule is satisfied.\n\nCan someone please answer - How would you design this system - DB schema, notification system, high level components to achieve\nscalability, fault tolence, achieve the SLO/SLI and which data structures would you use for optimized implementation?\n\nA moving average is a way to smooth out stock price data over a period of time so that you can see trends more clearly, instead\nof being distracted by small daily fluctuations.\nbasically average of stock price/day ",
      "fontSize": 20.859363725046993,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a system where a user can have X favourite stocks and has subscribed to their changes. User will set some rules for price drop/ price rise above a threshold or % value and if the rule is satisfied then we have to sent notificaiton to user.\n\nFor eg: let say user have subscribed to ABC stock and set rule that if stock price goes above 100$ send me notification.\n\nTypes of rules can be - opening price, current price, moving average, etc.\nUser should get the notification within a minute.\nSystem should be able to scan and check more than 1 million rules set by users and send notification if any rule is satisfied.\n\nCan someone please answer - How would you design this system - DB schema, notification system, high level components to achieve scalability, fault tolence, achieve the SLO/SLI and which data structures would you use for optimized implementation?\n\nA moving average is a way to smooth out stock price data over a period of time so that you can see trends more clearly, instead of being distracted by small daily fluctuations.\nbasically average of stock price/day ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "JGvTpjas9fQAUVbGRqfJV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20455.826751501492,
      "y": -7769.68548909446,
      "width": 2720.2293336468742,
      "height": 396.30380734948636,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bEC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1230198783,
      "version": 564,
      "versionNonce": 459651295,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "v07UjX--z0dZRnPxw4i57",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1763263202787,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FR: \n- user should be able to set rules over stock price. \n- user should be able to notify when these rules are satisfied.\n- type of rules -> \n     -current price -> less, greater, ge, le to current stock price. \n     -Notify me if ABC rises more than 5% today.” → (current_price - opening_price)/opening_price * 100 > 5\n     -Notify me if the current price crosses above the 5-day moving average.” Current price = $105, 5-day SMA = $102, Since 105 > 102 → notification is sent\n\nStock Price Events -> ? stockid, current price, opening price \ndo we have moving average ?? ",
      "fontSize": 31.70430458795891,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FR: \n- user should be able to set rules over stock price. \n- user should be able to notify when these rules are satisfied.\n- type of rules -> \n     -current price -> less, greater, ge, le to current stock price. \n     -Notify me if ABC rises more than 5% today.” → (current_price - opening_price)/opening_price * 100 > 5\n     -Notify me if the current price crosses above the 5-day moving average.” Current price = $105, 5-day SMA = $102, Since 105 > 102 → notification is sent\n\nStock Price Events -> ? stockid, current price, opening price \ndo we have moving average ?? ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2Kv7aq7wDYrPkMiZmCDAQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20475.857599100884,
      "y": -7270.188636293367,
      "width": 1569.14990234375,
      "height": 1664.4759908678427,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bEE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 665569311,
      "version": 1331,
      "versionNonce": 1855749009,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763263445903,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NFR:\n- how stock price change work ? \n- is it like per second or any time ? \n- also rule will be archived once notfication done ? -> no but at max 50notification/day\n- is it ok in worst case if get duplicate notification to user ? \n- how to delay is ok between price and notification ? -> since every price change we want \n  notify ? \n- scalable. \n- do we have fix metric of 5-day average ? or its variable ? \n- error handlng.\n- alerts and mnotirong and pager\n\nEstimations: \n- stocks count-> 10k \n- rules/user count -> 50\n- total rules -> 50*1m -> 50M\n- stock events/s -> count -> 100(peak)*10k -> 1M/s\n- latency , stock price -> notification -> under few seconds.\n- storage -> later. \n\nEntities: \n- user, rule, stock, event\n\nApi design: \n- Rule creation.\n/api/v1/rule     POST\nrequest: {RULE} , Respnose: {statuscode}\n- READ, UPDATE, DELETE.\n\nDatabase Schema: \n- User\n    - Id\n- RuleType\n    - Id\n    - type\n- Rule\n    - Id\n    - userId\n    - ruleTypeId\n    - status\n    - threshold\n    ",
      "fontSize": 31.70430458795891,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NFR:\n- how stock price change work ? \n- is it like per second or any time ? \n- also rule will be archived once notfication done ? -> no but at max 50notification/day\n- is it ok in worst case if get duplicate notification to user ? \n- how to delay is ok between price and notification ? -> since every price change we want \n  notify ? \n- scalable. \n- do we have fix metric of 5-day average ? or its variable ? \n- error handlng.\n- alerts and mnotirong and pager\n\nEstimations: \n- stocks count-> 10k \n- rules/user count -> 50\n- total rules -> 50*1m -> 50M\n- stock events/s -> count -> 100(peak)*10k -> 1M/s\n- latency , stock price -> notification -> under few seconds.\n- storage -> later. \n\nEntities: \n- user, rule, stock, event\n\nApi design: \n- Rule creation.\n/api/v1/rule     POST\nrequest: {RULE} , Respnose: {statuscode}\n- READ, UPDATE, DELETE.\n\nDatabase Schema: \n- User\n    - Id\n- RuleType\n    - Id\n    - type\n- Rule\n    - Id\n    - userId\n    - ruleTypeId\n    - status\n    - threshold\n    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
